// A2 course (A1 → A2 roadmap), module 5 „Linn, kohad ja tee” (a2-021…025), level A2. Lesson template v4
// (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12, docs/METHODOLOGY_STANDARD.md). One storyline, one year before the B1
// course (docs/COURSE_CAST.md): Sofia (27) has lived in Tallinn for a month (room at Malle Pärn's, Akadeemia tee 30,
// Mustamäe) and learns the town: the public transport card (ühiskaart, Tallinn residents ride free), the library card,
// a parcel from her mother Helgi in the parcel machine, Oskar's school, the Old Town. Keelekool Sõna (Narva maantee 7,
// Mon–Thu 9–12; teacher Maret, administrator Ene, classmates Lucía — architect from Valencia, Dmitri — bus driver,
// Tom — programmer from Ireland); Jaan cooks at café Pann (8–16, here placed in Kadriorg); Jaan's family lives at
// Männi 8 near Kase kool (Oskar 8, class 2; football Tue 17–18). Goal, said on the first sheet: at the end the learner
// guides a classmate by phone from the language school to the café and writes him a message with directions
// (024 Kasuta, final project).
//   021 errands in town — kus? kuhu? kust? with places (apteegis / apteeki / apteegist, raamatukokku,
//       postkontorisse, turul) and the first plural cases (poodides, parkides, kohvikutes, tänavatel) — grammar plan
//       „locatives” a2-021; a free Saturday with Jaan (plan, talk, message).
//   022 asking the way and checking it (Kas see on kaugel? Palun korrake!), tram and bus (sõidan trammiga, väljun
//       peatuses, istun ümber), kuni + -ni and üle + genitive; picking Oskar up from school; a closed street.
//   023 the imperative (sina: vaata, mine, ära oota; teie: vaadake, minge, ärge oodake) — grammar plan
//       „imperative” a2-023; lost in the Old Town with Lucía, the parcel machine, Kadri's instructions, Helgi at the
//       bus station and the ticket machine.
//   024 signs, opening hours (kella üheksast viieni, esmaspäevast reedeni) and a map; the service centre with
//       Viktor; guiding Tom to café Pann (final project; imperative and place forms again).
// Recycling of module 4 (kodu ja ümbrus): koju, kodus, poodi, linna, tuppa, toas, laual, esikus, külmkapis, põrand,
// katki, kõrval, vastas, lähedal, taga, peatus, linnaosa, vaikne, mööbel. Harno A2 formats trained: short-answer
// listening (played twice), dialogue T/F, phrases MC, signs matching, a letter with 3-option gaps, a ~150-word text
// with questions, a message ≥ 30 words, picture description. Lesson 5 is the module's check (unchanged).
// The v3 file is in archive/v3/a2/module05.js.
